<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Black interests buy control of South Africa's Tolcon.</title>
<headline>Black interests buy control of South Africa's Tolcon.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A black investment consortium has acquired a 51 percent controlling stake in South African toll road operator Tolcon from Murray and Roberts Holdings Ltd, local newspapers reported on Monday.  </p>
<p>Murray and Roberts Cobntractors director Malcolm Lobban said the sale -- for an undisclosed amount -- would create a new partnership to help meet South Africa's development needs.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
